# config/site.env.example
#
# Template. Copy to config/site.env and edit for this machine.
# The working copy (config/site.env) is gitignored — do not put real
# endpoints or tailnet hostnames in this file.
#
#   cp config/site.env.example config/site.env
#   # edit config/site.env for this host
#
# "Site" is a property of the host machine. The three URLs below are where
# this machine sends and reads telemetry; they are substituted into policies/
# at sandbox creation and written into the sandbox's /sandbox/.env.
#
# DEFAULT_PROFILE is also a property of the machine — a laptop that only ever
# does personal work should not need --profile personal on every command. It
# names a profile, not a credential; no tokens belong in this file.
#
# The three URLs are REQUIRED. sandbox.sh refuses to run if one is missing.
# A missing URL would make validate-profile.sh skip a check, and a skipped
# check reads the same as a passing one — an endpoint that is actually
# reachable would go unnoticed. DEFAULT_PROFILE is optional.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OTLP collector, as reached from inside a sandbox.
#
# Must be HTTP (4318), never gRPC (4317): OpenShell's egress proxy is
# HTTP/1.1 only and cannot carry HTTP/2. See docs/troubleshooting.md.
#
# Local podman stack (claude-otel-stack on the same host):
#   OTEL_URL=http://172.30.0.10:4318
#
# k3s cluster over Tailscale:
#   OTEL_URL=http://otel-collector.<tailnet>.ts.net:4318
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
OTEL_URL=http://172.30.0.10:4318

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telemetry query endpoints for this site. bin/validate-profile.sh probes
# these and compares the result against what the active profile's policy is
# supposed to grant — which differs per profile. These values say where the
# endpoints are, not whether any given sandbox may reach them.
#
# Full URLs rather than host/port pairs: the path differs per service, and
# Tailscale hostnames do not follow from the local addresses.
#
# Local podman stack:
#   PROMETHEUS_URL=http://172.30.0.11:9090/-/healthy
#   LOKI_URL=http://172.30.0.12:3100/ready
#
# k3s cluster over Tailscale:
#   PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.<tailnet>.ts.net:9090/-/healthy
#   LOKI_URL=http://loki-query.<tailnet>.ts.net/ready
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROMETHEUS_URL=http://172.30.0.11:9090/-/healthy
LOKI_URL=http://172.30.0.12:3100/ready

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default credential profile for this machine. Optional — leave unset for the
# work default. Lowest precedence: an explicit --profile wins, then the
# profile recorded in a sandbox's manifest.json, then this.
#
# Set to personal on a machine that never does work: it picks
# policies/personal.yaml, skips Jira/gcloud/gws credentials, and stops
# ensure_gws_creds from prompting for an OAuth flow you do not want.
#
#   DEFAULT_PROFILE=personal
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFAULT_PROFILE=
